{"symbol":"HUBN.SW","area":"europe","updated":"2026-11-16T18:22:45Z","info":{"address1":"Degersheimerstrasse 14","city":"Herisau","zip":"9100","country":"Switzerland","phone":"41 71 353 41 11","website":"https://www.hubersuhner.com","industry":"Communication Equipment","industryKey":"communication-equipment","industryDisp":"Communication Equipment","sector":"Technology","sectorKey":"technology","sectorDisp":"Technology","longBusinessSummary":"Huber+Suhner AG engages in the provision of power and data connectivity components and system solutions in Switzerland, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, the Asia-Pacific, and the Americas. It operates through three segments: Industry, Communication, and Transportation. The company offers antennas and antenna accessories; optical fiber connectors, coaxial connectors, optical fiber adapters, and coaxial adapters; optical fiber, coaxial, signal and control, power, databus, jumper, rolling stock, instrumentation, system, and hybrid cables; coaxial and optical fiber cable assemblies, hybrid and power assemblies and systems, and connection system for electric vehicles (EVs); and fiber cable management products, such as chassis, modules, fiber management accessories, optical distribution frames, and enclosures. It also offers components, including terminations, attenuators, filters, splitters and couplers, tappers, coaxial DC blocks, and surge protective devices; tools and accessories; pluggable transceivers and transceiver cables; and other systems, such as optical switches, RF-over-fiber solutions, ethernet switches, optical multiplexers, and CPE. In addition, the company provides e-business and supply management services, as well as RF Tools, an application that operates as a cable assembly calculator; injection moduling and plating services. It serves aerospace and defense, EV charging infrastructure, test and measurement, data center, fixed access network, mobile network, general industrial, automotive, railway, and other industry markets. Huber+Suhner AG was founded in 1864 and is headquartered in Herisau, Switzerland.","fullTimeEmployees":4488,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Urs  Ryffel","age":58,"title":"Chief Executive Officer","yearBorn":1967,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":1126000,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Richard  Haemmerli","age":48,"title":"Chief Financial Officer and Legal & Global Procurement","yearBorn":1977,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Alexander  Graf","age":54,"title":"Chief Information Officer","yearBorn":1971,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Christiane  Jelinek","age":48,"title":"Chief Communications Officer","yearBorn":1977,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Patricia  Stolz","age":56,"title":"Chief Human Resources Officer","yearBorn":1969,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Reto  Bolt","age":59,"title":"Chief Operating Officer of Industry Segment","yearBorn":1966,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Stefan  Metz","title":"Head Product Management & Development RF","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Stephan  Ott","title":"Head of R&D Low Frequency","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Drew  Nixon","age":60,"title":"Chief Operating Officer of Transportation Segment","yearBorn":1965,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Jurgen  Walter","age":57,"title":"Chief Operating Officer of Communication Segment","yearBorn":1968,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":84000,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0}],"auditRisk":5,"boardRisk":9,"compensationRisk":10,"shareHolderRightsRisk":10,"overallRisk":10,"governanceEpochDate":1793491200,"compensationAsOfEpochDate":176713920